{
  "id": "grammar.a1.08.03.querer",
  "title": "Querer and poder",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Say what you want",
      "content": "*Querer* means to want. You know stem-changing verbs from Unit 8: *querer* changes *e* to *ie* in every form except *nosotros*, so learn the common forms as a set."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Querer in the present",
      "rows": [
        [
          "yo",
          "quiero"
        ],
        [
          "tú",
          "quieres"
        ],
        [
          "él / ella / usted",
          "quiere"
        ],
        [
          "nosotros / nosotras",
          "queremos"
        ],
        [
          "ellos / ellas / ustedes",
          "quieren"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "items": [
        {
          "spanish": "Quiero una manzana.",
          "english": "I want an apple."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "¿Qué quieres?",
          "english": "What do you want?"
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Ella quiere pan.",
          "english": "She wants bread."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Queremos dos botellas de agua.",
          "english": "We want two bottles of water."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Say what you can do",
      "content": "*Poder* means can, to be able to. It changes *o* to *ue* in the same forms as *querer* changes *e* to *ie* (not in *nosotros*). Use it with an infinitive: *¿Puedo pagar aquí?*"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Poder in the present",
      "rows": [
        [
          "yo",
          "puedo"
        ],
        [
          "tú",
          "puedes"
        ],
        [
          "él / ella / usted",
          "puede"
        ],
        [
          "nosotros / nosotras",
          "podemos"
        ],
        [
          "ellos / ellas / ustedes",
          "pueden"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "items": [
        {
          "spanish": "¿Puedes ayudar, por favor?",
          "english": "Can you help, please?"
        },
        {
          "spanish": "No puedo comer pan.",
          "english": "I can't eat bread."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Podemos tomar una bolsa.",
          "english": "We can take a bag."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "content": "Use *querer* + a noun: *Quiero pan*. Use *querer* + an infinitive later when you want to say that you want to do something."
    }
  ]
}
